  haven't implemented anything.

  [1mThe main design decision:[0m the page is built from the Keel kit components in [38;5;153mvendor/kit/[39m ([38;5;153mpageHeader[39m, [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m,
  [38;5;153mselectField[39m, [38;5;153mdataTable[39m, [38;5;153mbadge[39m, [38;5;153memptyState[39m). It doesn't copy the hand-written markup in [38;5;153mservices.js[39m. The spec asks for
  sorting and filtering to behave like Services, and the kit already does exactly that:
  - Clicking the active column flips the sort direction.
  - Every other column starts ascending.
  - The sorted column gets [38;5;153maria-sort[39m and a ▲/▼ arrow.
  - The filter form submits itself when you change it and keeps the current sort in hidden fields.

  So the new page code is mostly configuration, and the plan doesn't modify [38;5;153mvendor/kit/[39m.

  [1mTwo tasks:[0m
  1. [1mPage renderer:[0m [38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m plus 9 rendering tests covering the header, the default newest-first order,
     sorting by Service both ways, sorting by Started, the status chips, the duration format, the filter keeping the
     sort, the empty state, and the fallback for unknown query values.
  2. [1mWiring:[0m the [38;5;153m/deploys[39m route in [38;5;153mserver.js[39m (which reuses the existing 503 handling), the nav link after Services, the
     README, and server tests. Those tests check the route, the nav order, and a 503 when [38;5;153mdeploys.json[39m is either missing
     or contains broken JSON.

  [1mGaps in the spec I filled in (listed in the plan under "Decisions the spec leaves open"):[0m
  - The query values are [38;5;153msort=service|startedAt[39m and [38;5;153mdir=asc|desc[39m. The default is [38;5;153mstartedAt[39m/[38;5;153mdesc[39m, so an unknown [38;5;153mdir[39m falls
    back to [38;5;153mdesc[39m, not to [38;5;153masc[39m as it does on Services.
  - With "All environments" selected and no deploys at all, the page says "No deploys".
  - The chip colors use the kit's badge colors. The kit's amber is a bit darker than the amber on the Services page, and
    I didn't plan any CSS changes to match them.

  [1mHow I checked it:[0m I pasted the plan's code into a scratch copy of the repo and ran the full suite: all 29 tests passed
  (18 existing plus 11 new). The Codex review gate was skipped because the Codex plugin isn't installed, and I recorded
